  "document_statements": [
    {
      "source_id": "firms_download_readme",
      "url": "https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/download/Readme.txt",
      "retrieved": "2026-11-14",
      "text": "The FIRMS download readme says a request can return near-real-time files, standard-quality files, or both, and that NRT data are replaced when standard data are available, after approximately three months. It defines fire_nrt_M-C61 as MCD14DL, fire_archive_M-C61 as standard-quality MCD14ML, fire_nrt_SV-C2 as VNP14IMGTDL, and fire_archive_SV-C2 as standard-quality VNP14IMGTML. It defines fire_nrt_J1V-C2 as VJ114IMGDL and fire_nrt_J2V-C2 as VJ214IMGDL. It does not define fire_archive_J1V-C2 or fire_archive_J2V-C2. It states: standard quality data is not yet available from FIRMS for NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. The characters after the product code are the download request id. The Collection / Version field is described as the way to distinguish MODIS from VIIRS when the files are combined, not as an NRT-versus-standard flag."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "firms_api_availability",
      "url": "https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/data_availability/",
      "retrieved": "2026-11-14",
      "text": "The FIRMS API data-availability page lists separate sensor codes for near-real-time and standard processing, including VIIRS_NOAA20_NRT, VIIRS_NOAA20_SP, VIIRS_NOAA21_NRT, VIIRS_NOAA21_SP, VIIRS_SNPP_NRT, VIIRS_SNPP_SP, MODIS_NRT, and MODIS_SP. Those codes are catalog labels. They are not columns in the local CSV files."
    }
  ],
